april the 2nd 2019  algerian president abdel aziz bhutahlir  resigned following weeks of massive  street protests  frail  unable to walk or talk and rarely seen  in public following a stroke he suffered  in 2013  but  bound to pressure from protesters and  the army chief  this is the moment he resigned and  handed over power to the senate speaker  who became the interim head of state  an undignified exit for the man who  played crucial roles in algeria's modern  history  buchalika is considered a national hero  by his supporters  he fought on the battlefield during  algeria's war of independence from  france then  served as foreign minister until 1979.  in the early 1980s he was accused of  corruption and went into self-imposed  exile the charges were later dropped  and at the end of the civil war in the  late 1990s that claimed the lives of  thousands butterflies won an election  with the backing of the military the  opposition said the vote was rigged  buttaflirca won praise for restoring  stability that led to an economic boom  and major development projects  nationwide he also managed to hold the  country together during the arab spring  there were protests in january 2011  against poverty and unemployment the  government responded by creating  thousands of small business  opportunities with generous incentives  to young entrepreneurs reducing food  prices and ending a decades-old state of  emergency  despite the initiatives riots continued  after winning a second mandate in 2004  but africa changed the constitution to  run for a third term  and despite deteriorating health he  changed the constitution once again to  secure a fourth term  western leaders considered him an  important ally in the fight against  armed groups in north africa but  afflicted had zero tolerance towards  al-qaeda and others  his heavy-handedness linked to that  approach is blamed for costing civilian  lives  in 2013  30 foreign workers were killed when  butterflier ordered the army to storm a  gas plant in the algerian desert  the aim was to rescue hundreds of  hostages held by an armed group  affiliated to al-qaeda  critics said the president could have  saved lives had he negotiated a safe  exit for the hostage years or planned  the counter-attack more carefully  but  grip on power started to slip when he  announced his bid to run for a fifth  term in february 2019.  hundreds of thousands of algerians  poured into the streets in the biggest  demonstrations seen since the  independence in 1962  for five weeks the protesters demanded  the president and his allies resign but  first tried to placate protesters by  reversing his decision to stand again  and postponing the election  saying he'd stay on until a new  constitution was adopted  but it wasn't enough to stop the revolt  the protests continued  was sealed when the army chief stepped  in forcing algeria's longest serving  president from power
 

